title: "Cloud session to main: how the work gets back to your PC"
---
%% SOURCE: a cloud session works on a fresh clone, no access to local files = code.claude.com/docs/en/scheduled-tasks.md, comparison table ("Access to local files | No (fresh clone)")
%% SOURCE: the session pushes claude/ branches = code.claude.com/docs/en/claude-code-on-the-web.md
%% SOURCE: "When a session completes, you can create a PR from claude.ai/code" = claude-code-on-the-web.md
%% SOURCE: claude --cloud "task" starts a cloud session from the CLI = claude-code-on-the-web.md
%% SOURCE: cloning and pull request creation require GitHub = claude-code-on-the-web.md, Limitations
%% SOURCE: the repo's remote is GitHub (example-org/garden-journal) = git remote -v
%% SOURCE: git pull --rebase replays your local commits on top of the remote's, then git push sends them = git-scm.com/docs/git-pull ("--rebase")
%% SOURCE: a pull or a rebase stops on a conflict and leaves it for you to resolve = git-scm.com/docs/git-pull
%% SOURCE: a plain git pull merges rather than rebases = git config pull.rebase=false
%% SOURCE-EXEMPT: "Files changed" and "Merge pull request" = standard GitHub UI labels, not checked against a live page this session
%% SOURCE-EXEMPT: "your-task" in the branch name is a placeholder
%% NOT CLAIMED: the exact label of the PR button in claude.ai/code -- the docs say "create a PR", not the button text
%% NOT CLAIMED: whether the session pushes as it goes or only at the end -- the docs say it pushes claude/ branches
sequenceDiagram
    participant you as You<br/>(your PC, your clone)
    participant main as GitHub<br/>main
    participant pr as GitHub<br/>pull request page
    participant branch as GitHub<br/>claude/your-task
    participant vm as Cloud session<br/>(Anthropic's machine)

    Note over you,vm: Start the job
    you->>main: 1 · commit + git push your work
    Note over you: type:<br/>claude --cloud "your task"
    you->>vm: 2 · this starts a cloud session
    main->>vm: 3 · fresh clone of main<br/>(sees only what you pushed)
    Note over vm: works:<br/>edits + commits
    vm->>branch: 4 · push to its own branch<br/>(main is untouched)

    alt Route A: merge on GitHub's website (recommended)
        branch->>pr: A1 · you create a PR (in claude.ai/code)
        you->>pr: A2 · review the Files changed tab
        Note over pr: Not happy?<br/>Close the PR unmerged:<br/>main stays as it was.
        pr->>main: A3 · Merge pull request
        main->>you: A4 · git pull<br/>(or git pull --rebase + git push<br/>if you have local commits)
    else Route B: ask Claude on your PC to merge it (no review page)
        branch->>you: B1 · git fetch + git merge
        you->>main: B2 · git push
    end

    Note over you,main: Conflict = both sides changed the same lines.<br/>git pull in A4 or git merge in B1 stops:<br/>ask Claude to resolve it.
